1fju|n|To grant; to acknowledge; to admit to be true; to confess; to recognize in a particular character; as, we own that we have forfeited your love.	N:1qqy,30,1~1qqy,30,1
1fju|a|Belonging to; belonging exclusively or especially to; peculiar; -- most frequently following a possessive pronoun, as my, our, thy, your, his, her, its, their, in order to emphasize or intensify the idea of property, peculiar interest, or exclusive ownership; as, my own father; my own composition; my own idea; at my own price. ; To hold as property; to have a legal or rightful title to; to be the proprietor or possessor of; to possess; as, to own a house.	j:1qqy,50,4;1psp,40,4;hda,39,5;1e6l,38,3;1vc0,37,5;qdb,36,5;1w0v,32,8;1vby,32,6;3d4,27,15;1hx0,25,1~3d4,27,15;1njd,21,13;1w0v,32,8;6r5,4,8;1lms,2,7;1vby,32,6;2168,9,6;jba,24,5;1vc0,37,5;hda,39,5
1fjw|n|One who owns; a rightful proprietor; one who has the legal or rightful title, whether he is the possessor or not.	a:1lht,88,5~1lht,88,5
